# React Components (Awesome-adapted · SPFx)

## Before creating
1. Search `src/webparts/**` and `src/shared/**` for existing component/pattern
2. Match neighbor web part: `*WebPart.ts` + `components/*.tsx` + `*.module.scss`
3. Prefer extending shared `src/shared/` primitives over duplicate markup

## New component checklist
- TypeScript props interface; default export only if file convention requires
- Styles: `*.module.scss` — no Tailwind/shadcn/v0 scaffold
- Fluent controls → `fluentui-gated` (v8 `@fluentui/react`)
- CMS copy: follow `techRiskCulture` / web part CMS patterns when applicable
- A11y: semantic elements, keyboard, focus — see `spfx/references/react-design.md`
- A11y (cont.): visible focus ring; sufficient contrast; semantic controls over div-click; ARIA only when native semantics are insufficient

## State & data
- Web part properties vs React state — don't duplicate source of truth
- List/Graph reads → `spfx-gated` + PnPjs patterns
- Side effects in `useEffect` with cleanup (timers, listeners, rAF)

## Reject
- v0.dev / shadcn / Tailwind generation links from upstream awesome rule
- v9 Fluent imports
- Porting game canvas into TSX render loop
